,"kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":96,"verse":23,"english":"O Vaidehi, beholding your face like to a lotus heated under the sun, or a lily that has been crushed, or like to gold covered with dust, or the moon enveloped by clouds, grief begot of this vortex of disaster that is in my mind, fiercely burns me, as fire consume a structure.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.935,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-104-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2096023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59bebefa8fdddbb4ae2cea5695fa86fc5d1a3517fc22cd814c2fce81d42d84a9","compact":"f2556da72db8d16e22da0d1f3b4e7f990c5c7753ab68bd248fabb166e6ee92dc","nasal":"0243ced63245fbf02a73215c259245c379646d8e1a000558b203976d4056e092"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-96-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":96,"verse":24,"english":"As his wretched mother was thus speaking, Bharata's elder brother, Räghava, approaching, took the feet of Vasiştha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.906,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-104-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2096024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be0b9dde4ca46e58b9665e3ae14c42bf7a46345bd79e28be667ba1bc98880004","compact":"0d03d8e6878f3ec97d37f05b9df9671f905840017244ba9e7b34ab20f20cca19","nasal":"265e9d7fd6ce885058d9c2c54c660b2a87e5b33ceeaef0b1457bd976a4e68eb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-96-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":96,"verse":25,"english":"Having taken hold of the feet of the priest resembling a flame, and of accumulated energy, like to that lord of the immortals, Indra, taking the feet of Bșhaspati, Rāghava sat down with him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.932,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-104-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2096025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","engli