age, will say to him?\", this intense curiosity arose in (the mind of) all the noble persons present there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-104-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2096028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ef428fa086288e2b9bdade44f4e9b5915d539440d1e83a67b4a7c61f7430f51","compact":"d6b6db1f95176a4136f97d078a56cf572d98a0ef57f6688599ac3a7832f6ddc1","nasal":"d6b6db1f95176a4136f97d078a56cf572d98a0ef57f6688599ac3a7832f6ddc1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-96-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":96,"verse":29,"english":"And Rāghava having truth and forbearance, and Lakşmaņa endowed with magnanimity, and Bharata possessed of righteousness, surrounded by their friends, appeared (there) like to the three fires surrounded by Sadasyas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.802,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-104-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2096029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7315f4a9914e35a1f5f374e3ad30479b8f07467d12d0988198460ba4d61d9f9","compact":"92cd14e7140aa19e9c4803e9bf3e3627401ab0b86983e628efa574bf500a7af4","nasal":"92cd14e7140aa19e9c4803e9bf3e3627401ab0b86983e628efa574bf500a7af4"}}]
